It's likely that the bag is still on the level.  A potion of object
detection (or a detect treasure spell) shows you all the objects 
on the level, even if they're in water.  However, there are a few
ways this spell might fail.

- If you're standing right next to it, and not blind, then you 
  will see it, but once you press -- more --, you'll only see 
  the water (so look carefully before hitting more, or else blind
  yourself before using the spell).

- Even if you do the detect object/treasure correctly, it won't 
  show you objects which are in pits which have been filled in
  (either with a boulder, or with water/lava).  However these objects
  are still reclaimable.

To reclaim objects in pits which have been filled in with something,
you must turn the square back into a pit.

If the pit is filled with water then either freeze the water or
push a boulder into it.  Before digging again with your pick-axe,
freeze all the surrounded water to make sure that the next hole
you dig doesn't also fill with water.  Once you've done that, dig
again with a pick-axe.  This will make a pit, and the lost object
should be in it.

If it is not in it, make sure that you froze/dug the correct square.
If you did, then you probably missed some message above where the 
object fell though the hole.  Try doing detect object/treasure
on the next level down.
